    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01HCZPNNZCNSFR58GBPNPW4VER\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to moderate product and store reviews in Klaviyo. Moderating allows you to publish all valid reviews while rejecting inappropriate or irrelevant reviews (e.g., reviews with offensive content).</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HCZPNNZCQV0661Z89T5RPEC1\">Before you begin</h2>\n<p>Customer reviews, including their collection and management, are governed by various regulators. <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/16685026123035\">Learn recommended best practices</a> for enabling transparency, fairness, and compliance throughout your reviews program.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HCZPNNZC97Y82J6GDAQ93AJS\">Set auto-approval settings</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Select the <strong>Reviews</strong> tab in Klaviyo.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Reviews settings</strong>.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Publishing rules and notifications</strong>.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720761655963\" alt=\"Publishing rules and notifications settings\" width=\"690\" height=\"354\">\n</li>\n<li>Choose your auto-approval settings: \n<ol>\n<li>Whether to auto-approve reviews.</li>\n<li>Which star ratings to auto-approve (e.g., approve all 4- and 5-star reviews, but require manual review for all others).</li>\n<li>Whether reviews with media (i.e., images) or profanity require manual approval.</li>\n<li>Whether reviews containing certain keywords (e.g., top-level domains like “.com”) should be flagged for manual approval to catch potential spam or links.</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>.<br>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/36274349748123\" alt=\"\" width=\"577\" height=\"398\"></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HCZPNNZCVSM2ZJP4SZGQAVCB\">Moderate reviews</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Select the <strong>Reviews</strong> tab in Klaviyo. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>All reviews</strong>. Here, you’ll see a list of all reviews. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Pending</strong> to only see reviews that require moderation.<br>\n<br>\nYou can also filter reviews by time period, rating, reply (i.e., <em>Includes reply</em> or <em>No reply</em>), and whether a review is verified. <br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720761662619\" alt=\"Pending reviews\" width=\"202\" height=\"299\">\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720773413659\" alt=\"Reviews moderation additional filters\" width=\"206\" height=\"280\">\n</li>\n<li>You have 2 options for every pending review: \n<ol>\n<li>Click <strong>Publish</strong> to publish the review publicly, or</li>\n<li>Open the <strong>Reject</strong> menu and select a rejection reason.<br>\n\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>Use discretion when rejecting reviews. For compliance purposes, it’s strongly recommended that you publish all reviews unless they meet one of the following criteria: <em>Profanity/Inappropriate</em>, <em>Contains private information</em>, <em>Unrelated to the product or service</em>, <em>False or misleading</em>, or <em>Fake</em>. You can also select <em>Other</em> if the reason doesn’t fall into one of the options above. When rejecting a review without text, you must provide a reason in the open text field. See our guide on <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/16685026123035\">best practices for collecting reviews</a> for more details on when it is acceptable to reject a review.</p>\n</div>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>Repeat the process with all pending reviews. Periodically review and publish or reject any with the <em>Pending</em> status (e.g., once per week).<br>\n<p>Review authors are not notified if their review is rejected. </p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>If auto-publish is turned on, any verified review with a <em>Pending</em> status is automatically published after 14 days to ensure accuracy and transparency. Learn about <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/16685026123035\">reviews regulations and best practices</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p>If you have a large number of pending reviews and want to publish them all at once, you can do this from the <strong>Overview</strong> tab. </p>\n<p>To publish all pending reviews at once: </p>\n</li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Reviews</strong> in Klaviyo. </li>\n<li>In the <em>Overview</em> tab, scroll to the <em>Pending activity</em> card. </li>\n<li>Open the additional options (3 dots) menu.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Publish all pending reviews</strong>.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/29565044594203\" alt=\"The option to publish all pending reviews\" width=\"624\" height=\"116\">\n</li>\n<li>In the modal that appears, confirm that you’re ready to publish all pending reviews.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"h_01J8QXBZ09XSYDD3QF6VZNH765\">Moderation and reviews without text </h3>\n<p>Many countries have <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/16685026123035\">regulations governing review moderation</a> which typically require brands to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Publish all legitimate reviews.</li>\n<li>Reject reviews only if they meet a specific set of criteria, such as:\n<ul>\n<li>Containing offensive language</li>\n<li>Including private information</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Exercise caution when rejecting reviews, especially those without text, to ensure compliance with these regulations.</p>\n<p>If a review without text doesn’t meet your auto-approval settings, it will be marked as <em>Pending</em> for 14 days, or until you publish it. If you are able to resolve the customer’s complaint during this period (e.g., through a <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/16680027976731\">customer service flow</a>) and the customer updates their review, only the updated review will be published.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h_01K1DRNRY23K20X2NN3Y63CFRG\">Moderate images</h3>\n<p>When moderating reviews with images, you have the following options: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Rotate</strong><br>\nIf the image is uploaded in the wrong orientation, rotate it so it appears correctly in reviews widgets. </li>\n<li>\n<strong>Hide</strong><br>\nIf an image is inappropriate or contains sensitive information, hide it so only the review text appears in reviews widgets. </li>\n</ul>\n<p>To moderate a review’s image:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Reviews &gt; All reviews</strong>. </li>\n<li>In the filter sidebar, select <strong>Photos</strong> to filter for reviews that include an image. <br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/39490614495899\" alt=\"\" width=\"322\" height=\"161\">\n</li>\n<li>Click the image you'd like to adjust. <br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/39490614499355\" alt=\"\" width=\"676\" height=\"276\">\n</li>\n<li>In the modal that appears, select <strong>Hide</strong> to hide the image anywhere the review appears publicly or <strong>Rotate</strong> to rotate the image counter-clockwise. <br>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/39490608143259\" alt=\"\" width=\"676\" height=\"223\"></p>",
